Language bench (galton_hoard/langbench)

The idea and the vocabulary of the language axis come from BabelArena
(QwenLM/BabelArena, Apache-2.0; paper arXiv 2609.23490): a tool task is
measured in more than one language, the strings of the task are typed as
Preserve, Translate-Free or Translate-Canonical, and a failure can be an
argument written in another language than the data (an empty search against a
localized catalogue).

No file, task or data of BabelArena is included in this repository. The 27 tasks,
the shop and family datasets, the BM25 search, the canonical entity map, the
language judge and every metric were written for this project, in Spanish and
English, and are covered by this repository's licence. The original is credited
here because the design follows it.
